-- title:
--   Pairwise coprime odd numbers in short windows (logarithmic form)
-- statement:
--   Let $d, X, H$ and $A_i$ ($i < d$) be natural numbers with $A_i + H \le X$. If
--
--   $$4\,(\log_2(4(d(\log_2 X + 1) + 1)) + 2)^2 \le \log_2 H$$
--
--   (integer binary logarithms), then there are pairwise coprime odd $s_i$ with $A_i < s_i \le A_i + H$. Thus windows of length $2^{O(\log^2 \log X)}$ suffice when $d$ is polylogarithmic in $X$.
--
